message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Stop Generating the Code You Already Have: Chimera Shared Edit Programs for Faster Long-Context Code Editing"
authors:
  - family-names: "Derinbogaz"
    given-names: "Ceyhun"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-28"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20428058"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cderinbogaz/chimera-shared-edit-programs-paper"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20428058"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Reproducible paper artifacts, figures, and summary benchmark data for Chimera
  shared edit programs, a representation-level acceleration approach for
  long-context code-editing inference. On 50 deterministic LongCodeBench-derived
  100K-context file-edit episodes, Chimera improves validated artifact throughput
  by 1.78x over normal vLLM unified diff and by 1.43x over an MTP-enabled
  unified-diff baseline.
keywords:
  - LLM inference
  - code editing
  - vLLM
  - multi-token prediction
  - long-context inference
  - edit programs
